And the poem (Jabberwocky) is actually the origin of both the Vorpal 
Sword and the creature Jabberwock. DnD took the term Vorpal to mean a 
weapon capable of decapitating creatures, and it probably entered 
NetHack from that source. The poem does not specifically say the blade 
decapitates the Jabberwock, only that it goes "snicker-snack" and with 
it's head, the hero goes "galumphing" back. In fact, the poem implies it 
takes more than one hit to kill the Jabberwock:

One, two! One, two! And through and through
The vorpal blade went snicker-snack!

You'd think if it were an instakill it would just be:

One! And through!
The vorpal blade went snicker!


